-- title:
--   Chart element with toric mathsf q-expansion and level automorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of level $\{q\ell\}$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity with $\zeta=\xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of `levelH q M'`, the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$, and let $K\subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ be the intermediate field $L$-generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁` of $\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A\to L\to K$, let $j\in K$ be non-zero with Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{Num}}$, and let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$. Then there are $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in both $\Gamma(\ell)$ and $\Gamma_0(M')$, an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` (so that on elements of $K$ given by ratios of integral $\mathsf q$-expansions of weight-$k$ forms for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, $\tau$ realises the slash action of `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`, for every embedding $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\zeta=e^{2\pi i/q}$), an element $H$ of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A K j` of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, Laurent series $u_1,u_2$ over $L$, units $c,\zeta',c'\in A^\times$ and $j_2\in\mathbb N$ such that: each $u_i$ is a ratio of $A$-integral power series with non-zero reduction modulo $\mathfrak m_A$, in the sense that $u_i\cdot y_i=x_i$ in $L((\mathsf q))$ for power series $x_i,y_i$ over $A$ whose residue reductions are non-zero; $1-c$ and $1-\zeta'c$ are units of $A$; $\zeta'-1\in\mathfrak m_A$; $0<j_2<q$; and, as Laurent series over $L$ (units pushed forward along $A\to L$), $H=u_1\bigl(x_T(\zeta'c)-x_T(c)\bigr)$ and $\tau H=u_2\bigl(x_T(c)-X(c',j_2)\bigr)$, where $x_T(\cdot)$ is the first coordinate of [`ModularCurve.tateToricPoint L q`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelPCusps.html#L20) and $X(\cdot,\cdot)$ the first coordinate of [`ModularCurve.nonToricPoint L q`](def/ModularCurve_TateSlots.html#L35).
--
--   This is the cusp-local step, in the Tate-curve description of the modular curve of level $H_1$ inside $q$-expansions, producing an element of the $j$-integral chart algebra whose $\mathsf q$-expansion is, up to a Gauss unit, a difference of abscissae of two toric points of the Tate curve, while its image under the level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ is a difference of a toric and a non-toric abscissa. It is used by the companion statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_isLevelAutAt_mem_chartAlgFin_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_and_apply_not_mem_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_isLevelAutAt_mem_chartAlgFin_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_and_apply_not_mem_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd), where these two expansions are compared with respect to the Gauss valuation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevelOne_exists_isLevelAutAt_mem_chartAlgFin_coe_eq_tateToricPoint_sub_and_apply_eq_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd.lean

